---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';

const title = 'Bible Bedtimes iOS Privacy Policy';
const description = 'How the Bible Bedtimes app for iPhone and iPad handles data, purchases, downloads and reminders.';
const canonical = 'https://biblebedtime.uk/privacy/bible-bedtimes-ios/';
const link = 'inline';
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical}>
  <Header />
  <main class="bg-night">
    <div class="wrap py-10 sm:py-16"><article class="measure min-w-0 [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">
      <p class="eyebrow">Bible Bedtimes · iPhone and iPad</p>
      <h1 class="h1-page mt-4">Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="small text-cream/70 mt-3">Last updated: 27 November 2026</p>

      <p class="lead mt-6">
        This policy covers only the <strong>Bible Bedtimes</strong> app for iPhone
        and iPad, with the bundle identifier
        <code class="text-[0.9em] break-words">uk.biblebedtime</code>. Signpost Digital Ltd
        is responsible for this app.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h3-page mt-10">Summary</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-cream/[0.82]">
        You don’t need an account, and there is no sign-in. The app shows no
        advertising, doesn’t track you across other apps or websites, and builds no
        profile of you. It contains no third-party analytics or crash-reporting kit.
        The current version of the app sends no usage counts.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h3-page mt-10">What stays on your device</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-cream/[0.82]">
        The app keeps these on your iPhone or iPad: your appearance choice, the
        stories and scriptures you save, the stories you played recently, where you
        stopped in a story, your sleep timer and autoplay choices, whether you last
        chose sound or video, a story you chose to hide from Tonight, whether the
        reminder is on and its time, that you have seen the welcome screen, which
        new stories you have already been shown, a count of finished stories used
        to decide when to ask for a rating, and any audio you choose to download.
        It also keeps a copy of the story list and the latest daily scripture, so it
        can open without a connection.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-cream/[0.82]">
        None of this is sent to us. Like any app’s settings, it can be part of your
        own iPhone or iPad backup; downloaded audio is left out of backups. You can
        remove a download from the story’s page in the app. Deleting the app removes
        everything it stored.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h3-page mt-10">Content, hosting and technical logs</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-cream/[0.82]">
        To show stories, audio, video, paintings and the daily scripture, the app
        fetches them over HTTPS from our own content service. It adds nothing about
        you to those requests: no name, email address, account, advertising
        identifier or listening history.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-cream/[0.82]">
        As with any web server, the content service and its network providers see
        the technical details needed to deliver the content, such as your IP
        address, the time and the file requested.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h3-page mt-10">Subscriptions and payments</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-cream/[0.82]">
        Premium is sold through Apple’s in-app purchase system. Apple takes the
        payment and holds your Apple account. The app learns from Apple which plan
        you have and whether it is still active, so it can unlock Premium; it never
        receives your card or bank details. Apple’s handling is covered by the
        <a class={link} href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/">Apple Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h3-page mt-10">Reminders</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-cream/[0.82]">
        The daily scripture reminder is optional. It is set only after you give
        permission, and your device schedules it itself. The app registers for no
        push notifications and uses no push service of its own.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h3-page mt-10">Ratings and sharing</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-cream/[0.82]">
        Now and then the app asks Apple to show its standard rating prompt. Apple
        decides whether it appears, and any rating you give goes to Apple. When you
        share a scripture or a prayer, the app passes its text and a link to the
        App Store to your device’s share sheet. You choose where it goes; the app
        isn’t told.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h3-page mt-10">Children</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-cream/[0.82]">
        The app asks nobody for personal details.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h3-page mt-10">Your choices and requests</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-cream/[0.82]">
        There is no account for us to delete. You can remove downloads in the app,
        or delete the app to remove everything it stored, and you can manage or
        cancel a subscription in your Apple account settings. For a privacy
        question, a request about your data, or help, use our
        <a class={link} href="/support/">support page</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h3-page mt-10">Changes</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-cream/[0.82]">
        We will update this policy before the app starts sending usage counts, or
        adds analytics, advertising, accounts, push notifications or any other
        material change to how it handles data. The date at the top shows the
        current version.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h3-page mt-10">Other policies</h2>
      <ul class="mt-3 text-cream/[0.82] list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 marker:text-gold">
        <li>
          The Spanish app:
          <a class={link} href="/privacy/bible-bedtime-espanol-ios/" lang="es">Política de privacidad de Bible Bedtime Español</a> (in Spanish).
        </li>
        <li>
          This website and our publishing tools:
          <a class={link} href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </article></div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
